From 7acf6ae5ec720f13fc5e7cbe7c2a351b43c3fadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:14:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: one always-on display model, Peek Display as the
 always-on screen

Always-on display:
- doze_always_on is only the user's switch. plait_doze_always_on_auto_mode
  says when it shows: 0 always, 1-4 schedules, 5 only while charging (new);
  plait_doze_on_charge now means "also while charging" outside a schedule
- AutoAODService no longer flips doze_always_on (and its override/prefs
  bookkeeping); it publishes plait_doze_always_on_schedule_active.
  AmbientDisplayConfiguration combines switch, mode, schedule and plug state
- Old settings migrate once (plait_aod_model=2): a schedule turns the switch
  on; "while charging" with the switch off becomes "only while charging"
- SystemUI DozeSuppressor moves DOZE <-> DOZE_AOD when plugging in or out or
  the schedule window opens or closes; before, AOD-on-charge only appeared at
  the next screen off and the schedule had to fake a pulse
- DozeParameters refreshes AOD availability (keyguard transitions, screen-off
  animation) on plug and schedule changes
- PowerManagerService does not wake on plug or unplug while dozing when the
  always-on display is or was showing (no lighting up in a pocket on unplug)

Peek Display:
- With the always-on display on, Peek Display draws the always-on screen:
  clock, date, a charging line and the icons stay up in DOZE_AOD, the clock
  follows the doze time tick and shifts every minute against burn-in
- Every pulse but fingerprint ones keeps it up and touchable; fingerprint
  pulses get the stock screen; no breathing while the always-on screen shows

